<title>USA: CTG Resources Announces First ISI.</title>
<headline>CTG Resources Announces First ISI.</headline>
<dateline>GREENWICH, Conn. 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>CTG Resources Inc said the first Intelligent Solutions Inc cogeneration system in Connecticut Natural Gas Corp's service territory has become operational and is producing power for the YMCA in Greenwich.</p>
<p>The 60 kilowatt cogenerator uses natural gas and will replace 47 percent of the YMCA's commercial electric requirements, while also providing domestic hot water for the facility's operations, CTG said. It is the holding company of Connecticut Natural Gas.</p>
<p>The cogenerators are designed by ISI and are manufactured by MagneTek Inc.</p>
<p>Greenwich is served by United Illuminating Co.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
</text>
